{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add the core built-in plan-review criterion T15 \"overlay-derisk\". Stack-agnostic; LLM-routed on plan content via `overlay_routing: llm`, dispatched by the review orchestrator exactly like T13/T14 (there is no ticket-tag routing). The full rubric is specified verbatim below so the artifact can be authored without resolving any other ticket.\n\n## Rubric to write verbatim into src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T15.md\nYAML front-matter: `category: plan-review-criterion`, `execution_mode: AGENT`, `dimension: overlay-derisk`.\nBody:\n\nOVERLAY — apply only when ALL of the following hold; else PASS not-applicable.\n- S1 Codified loop? the mechanism is delivered/validated by pushing through an automated pipeline or an environment/infrastructure apply, not by running or unit-testing code directly.\n- S2 Slow or costly pass? one pass through that loop is slow (minutes-to-hours) or otherwise costly to run.\n- S3 Runtime-only correctness? the change introduces behavior whose correctness only resolves when it actually runs in a realistic environment (boots, authenticates, connects, is authorized, passes readiness) — unreachable by static/unit checks.\n\nWhen applicable, report a finding for each check not satisfied:\n- (a) RISK NAMED — the plan identifies the specific mechanism(s) confirmable only by completing the full loop.\n- (b) FAST OUT-OF-LOOP PROOF — for each named risk, the plan commits to proving it via the fastest feedback path available for that mechanism, outside the slow loop: running the unit locally/emulated where feasible, OR a manual experiment directly against the real target (an interactive call, a one-off CLI/console action, a probe script, a throwaway resource) where local reproduction isn't possible. The experiment is concrete and returns a verdict in minutes, not a delivery cycle. An unnamed \"we'll verify\" / \"we'll check after deploy\" does not satisfy it.\n- (c) PROVE-THEN-CODIFY — the cheap experiment comes before committing the mechanism into the slow loop, so the loop validates an already-proven mechanism.\n- (d) SCOPED CLEANUP — throwaway experiments are cleaned up afterward, with teardown that removes ONLY the artifacts the experiment itself created (the records a probe inserted, the scratch resource it spun up) and touches nothing pre-existing, shared, or persistent; a cleanup step that could delete, reset, or truncate a resource the experiment did not create (e.g. dropping an existing table or wiping a bucket to \"reset\" it) fails this check.\n\nANTI-FP: a manual experiment against the real target is a fully valid proof — never penalize choosing it over local reproduction; many stacks cannot be reproduced locally. A mechanism already proven elsewhere in the codebase needn't be re-proven.\n\n## Routing entry to add to src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json (key \"T15\")\n- `exec`: \"AGENT\"\n- `facet`: \"overlay-derisk\"\n- `overlay_routing`: \"llm\"  (orchestrator-dispatched content routing, as T13/T14)\n- `applies_at`: { \"suppress_types\": [\"bug\"] }\n- Posture/threshold: NOT set here — inherit the registry default (advisory). Advisory-vs-blocking is decided by the normal registry/review process, out of scope for this ticket.\n\n## Implementation steps\n1. Create src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T15.md with the front-matter + body above.\n2. Add the \"T15\" routing entry above to src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json.\n3. Add \"T15\" to CANONICAL_LLM in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py.\n4. Regenerate the guide: `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` (updates docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md).\n\n## Scope boundary\nThis ticket authors the criterion artifact + registration + regenerated guide only. Runtime routing/finder BEHAVIOR (does T15 fire on an infra plan and stay silent on an app-only plan) is proven by the eval-fixtures story 36ab-b649-b72b-4608, which depends on this ticket — not asserted here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T15.md exists containing the S1-S3 gate, checks (a)-(d), and the ANTI-FP paragraph verbatim, with front-matter `execution_mode: AGENT` and `dimension: overlay-derisk`.\n- [ ] `grep '\"T15\"' src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json` shows a routing entry with exec AGENT, facet overlay-derisk, overlay_routing llm, and applies_at.suppress_types [\"bug\"].\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar.llm.plan_review.registry import CANONICAL_LLM; assert 'T15' in CANONICAL_LLM\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] `rebar explain T15` prints the criterion name, exec tier AGENT, facet overlay-derisk, and the rubric body.\n- [ ] Registry validators pass: `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry` coverage/routing/guide checks (check_registry_coverage, validate_routing, validate_criteria_guide) report no orphans or missing prompt/routing for T15.\n- [ ] After `regenerate-criteria-guide`, `grep -A2 '^## T15' docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` shows the generated T15 section matching the rubric."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1784920539221773001,"uuid":"dc72682a-db78-4af5-a21d-03e7f8a6dbc4"}